1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:05,565
This is Arisan: savings circles on
your phone, run by a Solana program,

2
00:00:05,565 --> 00:00:06,437
not a person.

3
00:00:07,137 --> 00:00:12,837
Everyone pays in each round, and each
round one person takes the whole pot.

4
00:00:13,537 --> 00:00:17,653
Ana creates a circle: three
seats, 0.1 SOL a round,

5
00:00:17,653 --> 00:00:21,123
and a small stake she
gets back at the end.

6
00:00:21,823 --> 00:00:27,995
She gets an invite code, takes the first
seat and stakes from her own wallet.

7
00:00:28,695 --> 00:00:32,875
Budi and Citra join with
the code and stake too.

8
00:00:32,875 --> 00:00:36,795
With every seat taken,
Ana starts the circle.

9
00:00:37,715 --> 00:00:43,290
Round one: everyone pays 0.1 SOL
with one tap, right from Home.

10
00:00:43,990 --> 00:00:48,530
When the round ends, anyone
can run the draw: commit,

11
00:00:48,530 --> 00:00:53,756
then draw from a block hash
nobody knew. This time, Ana wins.

12
00:00:55,172 --> 00:01:00,150
The vault pays her on the spot,
and the history keeps every round.

13
00:01:00,850 --> 00:01:07,378
Round two goes to Citra, who ran the
draw herself. Round three goes to Budi.

14
00:01:07,378 --> 00:01:09,784
Each seat wins exactly once.

15
00:01:12,647 --> 00:01:15,584
Then everyone takes their stake back.

16
00:01:15,584 --> 00:01:19,393
In 0.3 SOL, out 0.3 SOL:
no lender, no interest.

17
00:01:20,093 --> 00:01:25,993
Arisan is live on Solana devnet.
Try it at arisan-self.vercel.app.

